      "explanation": "<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1leywsbat/0f041d5f-eac1-4098-ae93-83ee6789dd05/82dcf290-bd43-11ed-925b-0b030bfa420d/file-1leywsbay.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1leywsbat/0f041d5f-eac1-4098-ae93-83ee6789dd05/82dcf290-bd43-11ed-925b-0b030bfa420d/file-1leywsbay.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2023 (Online) 1st February Morning Shift Chemistry - Hydrocarbons Question 78 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1leywsbat/0f041d5f-eac1-4098-ae93-83ee6789dd05/82dcf290-bd43-11ed-925b-0b030bfa420d/file-1leywsbay.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1leywsbat/0f041d5f-eac1-4098-ae93-83ee6789dd05/82dcf290-bd43-11ed-925b-0b030bfa420d/file-1leywsbay.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1leywsbat/0f041d5f-eac1-4098-ae93-83ee6789dd05/82dcf290-bd43-11ed-925b-0b030bfa420d/file-1leywsbay.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1leywsbat/0f041d5f-eac1-4098-ae93-83ee6789dd05/82dcf290-bd43-11ed-925b-0b030bfa420d/file-1leywsbay.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1leywsbat/0f041d5f-eac1-4098-ae93-83ee6789dd05/82dcf290-bd43-11ed-925b-0b030bfa420d/file-1leywsbay.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1leywsbat/0f041d5f-eac1-4098-ae93-83ee6789dd05/82dcf290-bd43-11ed-925b-0b030bfa420d/file-1leywsbay.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n\n<br>cis-2-butene is more polar that is why it's solubility is more than trans-2-butene.\n<br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> A is correct.\n<br><br>cis-2-butene has a lower melting point than trans-2-butene as trans-form has compact packing crystal lattice. cis-2-butene is polar so, it has higher boiling point than trans-form.\n<br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> B is also correct.\n<br><br>cis-2-butene is more polar but dipole moment of cis-2-butene(A) is not zero.\n<br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> C is incorrect.\n<br><br>'Cis' structure is less stable than 'Trans\" structure. Less stable means more reactive. So Cis - But-2-ene(A) will react more easily with Br<sub>2</sub>.\n<br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> D is also incorrect."
